{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Seizes a dog by the ears</b> — it lacks a kaf: like one who seizes a dog by the ears, which is improper to do, so is one who meddles in a quarrel not his own." "And meddles — grows angry in a quarrel; and the measure of anger is that it has passed beyond the measure of will."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:53.153836473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}